refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.description;
public Time\DurationTime\Duration::multiplyBy intfactor
Returns a duration that is factor times as long as this duration. The sign of the duration is preserved.

&reftitle.parameters;
factor
The factor to multiply by. Must be greater than or equal to 0; a factor of 0 results in a duration of zero.

&reftitle.errors;
This method throws a ValueError if factor is negative.
A Time\TimeException is thrown if the resulting duration exceeds the maximum length of a duration.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Time\Duration::multiplyBy example


<?php
var_dump(Time\Duration::fromMilliseconds(1500)->multiplyBy(4));

try {
    Time\Duration::fromHours(1)->multiplyBy(3_000_000);
} catch (Time\TimeException $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}


